1
00:00:05,125 --> 00:00:06,083
LAND OF GOLDEN-EYED MONSTERS

2
00:00:06,083 --> 00:00:07,208
LAND OF GOLDEN-EYED MONSTERS
- Lis, isn't it hard to handle
all that luggage by yourself?

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:10,083
Lis, isn't it hard to handle
all that luggage by yourself?

4
00:00:11,083 --> 00:00:12,208
I'll be fine.

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:17,000
The less the rest of you have to carry,

6
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:19,166
the greater my chances of survival.

7
00:00:19,208 --> 00:00:22,041
So please let me take this.

8
00:00:22,041 --> 00:00:25,041
I'd like to respect Lis's wishes.

9
00:00:25,083 --> 00:00:26,083
All right.

10
00:00:26,166 --> 00:00:29,208
You're a part of our
mercenary band too, after all.

11
00:00:29,208 --> 00:00:31,208
If you get tired, don't hesitate to say so.

12
00:00:32,041 --> 00:00:33,166
Right!

13
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:36,125
I'm counting on you to watch
our surroundings, Piggymaru.

14
00:00:40,041 --> 00:00:43,208
We're good on food and water.

15
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Our greatest challenge is...

16
00:00:50,166 --> 00:00:51,208
Stick to the plan.

17
00:00:58,166 --> 00:01:00,083
Now come on out!

18
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:08,041
It's similar to the reptilian monsters
I fought in the Ruins of Disposal.

19
00:01:08,041 --> 00:01:10,208
The difference is that seaweed-like head...

20
00:01:10,208 --> 00:01:12,166
Is it a seaweed-headed lizard?

21
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:21,041
Paralyze!

22
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Poison.

23
00:01:27,166 --> 00:01:28,125
Good work.

24
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:31,125
Did you achieve what you wanted, Tooka?

25
00:01:31,166 --> 00:01:34,125
Yeah, we've cleared the first step.

26
00:01:34,125 --> 00:01:35,125
Sleep.

27
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:39,000
I wasn't sure my skill would work on
the creatures in the Land of Monsters,

28
00:01:39,041 --> 00:01:42,166
but Poison, Paralyze, and Sleep
all seem to be effective.

29
00:01:47,125 --> 00:01:48,125
They're inferior.

30
00:01:48,166 --> 00:01:49,125
Hmm?

31
00:01:49,125 --> 00:01:50,208
They look similar,

32
00:01:50,208 --> 00:01:53,166
but compared to the monsters
I faced in the Ruins of Disposal,

33
00:01:53,166 --> 00:01:55,125
these guys are far inferior in strength.

34
00:01:55,166 --> 00:02:00,208
So it seems the monsters in the so-called
Land of Monsters aren't too tough.

35
00:02:03,083 --> 00:02:04,125
If this is all they've got,

36
00:02:04,166 --> 00:02:06,000
they're no match for me.

37
00:02:06,041 --> 00:02:08,166
Sir Tooka, what are you doing?

38
00:02:09,041 --> 00:02:12,083
I think I saw this guy
somewhere in this book.

39
00:02:16,125 --> 00:02:19,000
Um, is this it?

40
00:02:19,041 --> 00:02:20,125
Yeah, that's him.

41
00:02:20,166 --> 00:02:24,166
Apparently this seaweed-esque bit
is an ingredient for a forbidden item.

42
00:02:24,166 --> 00:02:28,041
Something like the voice-altering
stone in the Lord of the Flies' mask?

43
00:02:28,041 --> 00:02:29,083
That's right.

44
00:02:31,166 --> 00:02:33,125
If you're interested, you can take it.

45
00:02:33,208 --> 00:02:35,041
Are you sure?

46
00:02:35,125 --> 00:02:37,041
I know I don't have to worry with you.

47
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:39,125
Thank you.

48
00:02:40,083 --> 00:02:43,041
Everyone's happy to get special treatment,

49
00:02:43,041 --> 00:02:44,125
and that wasn't a lie.

50
00:02:44,166 --> 00:02:48,208
Seras would see right through me
if I didn't mind my words carefully.

51
00:02:49,125 --> 00:02:53,000
All right, time to begin our conquest
of the Land of Golden-Eyed Monsters.

52
00:04:29,125 --> 00:04:33,166
LAND OF THE GOLDEN-EYED MONSTERS

53
00:04:35,166 --> 00:04:37,000
Thanks for the save.

54
00:04:38,208 --> 00:04:40,041
You're next, Lis.

55
00:04:40,041 --> 00:04:41,208
Coming, Sir Tooka!

56
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:45,041
You can slip on the stones, so be careful.

57
00:04:45,041 --> 00:04:46,000
I will.

58
00:04:46,041 --> 00:04:49,166
Tooka, shouldn't I just carry her over?

59
00:04:49,166 --> 00:04:52,000
She wants to do it herself.

60
00:04:52,041 --> 00:04:54,041
So we should respect that, right?

61
00:04:54,083 --> 00:04:57,166
Even so, what if she should slip?

62
00:04:57,166 --> 00:04:59,166
I-I'll be all right.

63
00:04:59,166 --> 00:05:05,166
I know I can't keep relying
on you for everything, Big Sis!

64
00:05:08,125 --> 00:05:11,125
Th-Thank you, little Piggymaru.

65
00:05:12,083 --> 00:05:15,083
So you had a safety measure
in place from the start?

66
00:05:15,083 --> 00:05:16,083
Well, you know...

67
00:05:16,166 --> 00:05:21,041
I want to do all I can to support Lis
when she puts her mind to something, too.

68
00:05:21,125 --> 00:05:24,166
She was in a situation similar
to what I went through long ago.

69
00:05:24,166 --> 00:05:27,000
Tooka, are you saying...?

70
00:05:27,041 --> 00:05:29,125
Yeah, I'm really just doing this for myself.

71
00:05:29,125 --> 00:05:30,125
Hmm...

72
00:05:30,125 --> 00:05:32,125
Wh-What's the matter?

73
00:05:32,125 --> 00:05:34,000
It's nothing.

74
00:05:34,041 --> 00:05:38,000
Though you should be mindful when
people say something like that.

75
00:05:38,041 --> 00:05:41,125
It tends to mean they were talking about
something they didn't want you to hear.

76
00:05:41,125 --> 00:05:43,083
Big Sis, is that true...?

77
00:05:43,125 --> 00:05:46,208
Um, I know I failed to make it across, but...

78
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:50,166
No. We certainly weren't talking about that.

79
00:05:51,166 --> 00:05:55,041
You don't often hear about children
born between elves and humans,

80
00:05:55,041 --> 00:05:59,125
much less children born
to high elf and human parents.

81
00:05:59,125 --> 00:06:03,041
So we were discussing what
a child born to Tooka and Seras

82
00:06:03,083 --> 00:06:05,041
would be like if that happened.

83
00:06:06,125 --> 00:06:08,041
Miss Seras?!

84
00:06:10,041 --> 00:06:12,041
Are you sure you don't want to dry them out?

85
00:06:12,125 --> 00:06:14,166
Yes, I'm sorry about this.

86
00:06:14,208 --> 00:06:17,208
I got distracted and let my guard down.

87
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:19,166
How embarrassing of me.

88
00:06:19,208 --> 00:06:22,041
So even you get distracted sometimes, hmm?

89
00:06:23,083 --> 00:06:26,125
I can't tell if this leopardman
is sharp or dense.

90
00:06:29,083 --> 00:06:31,125
We can't have you catch a cold.
At least wear this.

91
00:06:31,166 --> 00:06:34,000
Huh? Oh, no, I'm fine.

92
00:06:34,125 --> 00:06:35,125
Go on.

93
00:06:35,125 --> 00:06:38,125
Then... I hope you don't mind me borrowing it.

94
00:06:39,041 --> 00:06:41,041
I wash it pretty regularly.

95
00:06:41,083 --> 00:06:44,000
Oh, please, don't worry about that.

96
00:06:44,041 --> 00:06:46,083
You don't mind 'cause it smells like me?

97
00:06:46,125 --> 00:06:47,166
Precisely.

98
00:06:48,083 --> 00:06:49,041
I see.

99
00:06:49,208 --> 00:06:52,000
I meant that as a joke.

100
00:06:52,125 --> 00:06:55,000
I meant that as a joke, but...

101
00:06:57,208 --> 00:06:58,166
What's the matter?

102
00:07:00,041 --> 00:07:01,041
We're turning back, Lis.

103
00:07:01,083 --> 00:07:02,041
Huh?

104
00:07:02,041 --> 00:07:03,125
They found us. Tooka!

105
00:07:03,166 --> 00:07:05,000
Lis, over here.

106
00:07:06,125 --> 00:07:07,208
Monsters you recognize?

107
00:07:07,208 --> 00:07:08,166
Yeah.

108
00:07:08,208 --> 00:07:11,000
Sorry, I can't beat these.

109
00:07:11,041 --> 00:07:12,000
I see.

110
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:19,041
Are these what forced you and Lis
to flee the Land of Monsters?

111
00:07:20,041 --> 00:07:21,166
Your orders, Tooka?

112
00:07:21,208 --> 00:07:23,083
Stand back this time.

113
00:07:23,083 --> 00:07:24,125
Understood.

114
00:07:25,125 --> 00:07:28,125
I don't have time to prepare
my combo attack with Piggymaru.

115
00:07:46,166 --> 00:07:49,041
I see. You guys are...

116
00:07:49,208 --> 00:07:53,041
You're opponents not even the greatest
bloodsport warrior could defeat!

117
00:07:53,125 --> 00:07:54,166
Welcome...

118
00:07:54,166 --> 00:07:55,208
into my range!

119
00:07:56,083 --> 00:07:57,125
Paralyze!

120
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:00,166
I won't give you a real fight.

121
00:08:02,166 --> 00:08:07,166
You gleefully made your way here upon
spotting the prey you'd once let get away,

122
00:08:07,166 --> 00:08:10,125
not realizing you were the ones
being hunted this time.

123
00:08:10,208 --> 00:08:11,208
Berserk.

124
00:08:12,041 --> 00:08:13,041
Berserk.

125
00:08:18,166 --> 00:08:21,041
Sorry, but I'm finishing you off quick.

126
00:08:25,041 --> 00:08:26,166
TOOKA MIMORI
- You have leveled up.

127
00:08:26,166 --> 00:08:28,125
TOOKA MIMORI
- Finally gained another level, did I?

128
00:08:28,166 --> 00:08:30,083
Now then, Tooka...

129
00:08:30,083 --> 00:08:31,083
Before the fight,

130
00:08:31,125 --> 00:08:35,166
you sounded as if you knew of
these monsters from somewhere.

131
00:08:36,041 --> 00:08:38,125
They're probably nazorts.

132
00:08:39,083 --> 00:08:40,166
Just as I thought.

133
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:43,208
Tooka...

134
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:47,083
D-Don't tell me you plan
on eating that thing.

135
00:08:47,125 --> 00:08:49,000
Don't get the wrong idea, Eve.

136
00:08:49,041 --> 00:08:51,125
It's in Forbidden Arts: Complete Works,
which I borrowed.

137
00:08:52,041 --> 00:08:56,083
As I recall, it's one of the ingredients
for enhancing slimes like Piggymaru.

138
00:08:56,125 --> 00:08:58,000
- Isn't it?
- Yeah.

139
00:08:58,125 --> 00:09:00,041
So that's what you're up to?

140
00:09:00,083 --> 00:09:01,041
Hmm.

141
00:09:01,083 --> 00:09:06,125
So Piggymaru will be the one ingesting
that creepy, spongy substance.

142
00:09:08,125 --> 00:09:10,000
It's fine.

143
00:09:10,041 --> 00:09:13,125
Once the enhancement solution is finished,
it won't look like this.

144
00:09:15,083 --> 00:09:16,041
Probably.

145
00:09:17,166 --> 00:09:18,166
Sir Tooka?

146
00:09:18,166 --> 00:09:19,166
What?

147
00:09:21,166 --> 00:09:23,083
Eve, can you sense anything?

148
00:09:23,083 --> 00:09:24,166
I'm not sure.

149
00:09:24,208 --> 00:09:26,125
There was definitely a monster,

150
00:09:26,166 --> 00:09:27,125
but it was so brief.

151
00:09:27,166 --> 00:09:28,125
Seras?

152
00:09:28,125 --> 00:09:30,041
My spirits aren't responding either.

153
00:09:30,041 --> 00:09:31,166
But something's there, no doubt.

154
00:09:32,041 --> 00:09:33,041
And very close.

155
00:09:33,041 --> 00:09:35,083
There's no malice or hostility.

156
00:09:35,125 --> 00:09:36,083
Where is it?

157
00:09:38,166 --> 00:09:39,208
What?

158
00:09:41,125 --> 00:09:42,125
It's coming from me?

159
00:09:47,041 --> 00:09:48,166
Sir Tooka, that's...

160
00:09:49,041 --> 00:09:50,000
Yeah.

161
00:09:51,208 --> 00:09:53,166
I guess it's about to hatch?

162
00:10:05,166 --> 00:10:06,208
A-A horse?

163
00:10:06,208 --> 00:10:07,208
Hey, Eve...

164
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:11,125
I feel like it got even bigger after hatching.

165
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:15,125
You noticed that too?

166
00:10:15,125 --> 00:10:17,125
Is it a type of monster?

167
00:10:17,125 --> 00:10:21,125
I know of several equine monsters, but this...

168
00:10:21,166 --> 00:10:23,166
So not even you know it, huh?

169
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:26,041
Sir Tooka!

170
00:10:26,083 --> 00:10:27,041
It's all right.

171
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:31,166
It has no hostility toward us.

172
00:10:32,083 --> 00:10:33,166
A pony...

173
00:10:35,125 --> 00:10:37,125
Hmm? What's this?

174
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:39,083
Pardon me.

175
00:10:39,125 --> 00:10:42,125
This? It's an organ for absorbing magic.

176
00:10:42,166 --> 00:10:46,041
It's a unique feature often found
in monsters and magical creatures.

177
00:10:46,041 --> 00:10:47,083
I see...

178
00:10:47,125 --> 00:10:50,125
Could everyone but Piggymaru get back?

179
00:10:50,166 --> 00:10:53,041
And Eve, can I ask you to keep
an eye on our surroundings?

180
00:10:53,166 --> 00:10:59,000
This little one might have increased in size
from absorbing the magic in the area.

181
00:10:59,125 --> 00:11:00,125
And in that case...

182
00:11:02,125 --> 00:11:03,083
Does that bother you?

183
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:07,125
TOOKA MIMORI
E-CLASS HERO

184
00:11:09,125 --> 00:11:11,125
TOOKA MIMORI
E-CLASS HERO

185
00:11:18,125 --> 00:11:19,125
It's...

186
00:11:24,041 --> 00:11:25,208
The horse is amazing!

187
00:11:25,208 --> 00:11:26,208
I see.

188
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:30,125
So it possesses the ability
to transform by absorbing magic.

189
00:11:30,208 --> 00:11:34,000
You consume roughly a thousand MP
for your transformation, huh?

190
00:11:34,125 --> 00:11:37,125
This size seems perfect for hauling luggage.

191
00:11:38,041 --> 00:11:40,083
Hold on, do you want me to...

192
00:11:41,083 --> 00:11:43,166
You want me to pour even
more magic into you?

193
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:47,125
All right. Here I go.

194
00:11:48,125 --> 00:11:51,125
Ninety-five hundred...
ninety-six... ninety-seven...

195
00:11:52,041 --> 00:11:53,041
Ten thousand!

196
00:12:03,041 --> 00:12:05,208
We may have just added an
interesting companion to our group.

197
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:08,083
Maybe it thinks of me as a parent.

198
00:12:08,083 --> 00:12:11,208
It's part of our group?
Um, what are we going to name it?

199
00:12:12,041 --> 00:12:13,083
Good question...

200
00:12:13,083 --> 00:12:14,208
It's a fantastical horse.

201
00:12:15,083 --> 00:12:16,208
With eight legs.

202
00:12:18,083 --> 00:12:19,125
Slei...

203
00:12:20,125 --> 00:12:24,208
The horse that Odin once rode,
the divine beast Sleipnir.

204
00:12:25,083 --> 00:12:27,000
How about Slei?

205
00:12:29,041 --> 00:12:31,083
It appears to approve.

206
00:12:31,166 --> 00:12:34,125
We're happy to have you, Slei.

207
00:12:34,125 --> 00:12:35,083
Huh?

208
00:12:35,125 --> 00:12:36,125
S-Slei?!

209
00:12:36,166 --> 00:12:38,208
I-I'd prefer you not do that there...

210
00:12:39,125 --> 00:12:41,208
Seems it's taken a liking to you.

211
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:45,083
By the way, can you return
to your original form?

212
00:12:46,166 --> 00:12:48,166
I see. That's a relief.

213
00:12:48,208 --> 00:12:51,125
Don't just feel relieved! Please stop it!

214
00:12:55,125 --> 00:12:58,208
I'm sorry. This is all because we're weak.

215
00:12:58,208 --> 00:13:01,166
No, you're all doing your best.

216
00:13:01,166 --> 00:13:04,208
Good, good. Everyone's leveling
up at a nice pace.

217
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:07,000
All because of you, Asagi.

218
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:09,041
My group is talented.

219
00:13:09,041 --> 00:13:11,166
We coordinate to snuff out monsters,

220
00:13:11,166 --> 00:13:14,125
and in the end, we split the
experience like good friends.

221
00:13:14,125 --> 00:13:18,000
Thanks to that, even our
timid little pigeon is leveling up.

222
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:19,166
Th-Thank you.

223
00:13:23,041 --> 00:13:25,208
What's got you so on edge, Takuto?

224
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:27,041
I don't like this.

225
00:13:27,041 --> 00:13:28,000
Huh?

226
00:13:28,041 --> 00:13:32,125
They keep throwing weaklings at us, giving us
nothing but experience to appease us.

227
00:13:32,166 --> 00:13:34,166
Like lessons for little children.

228
00:13:34,208 --> 00:13:37,208
They've grossly underestimated me.

229
00:13:37,208 --> 00:13:42,000
I'll need to teach those top fighters

230
00:13:42,125 --> 00:13:44,041
just who I am.

231
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:51,083
Dangerous ones are on the way.

232
00:13:51,125 --> 00:13:56,125
This feels likely to be too much
for the heroes to handle right now.

233
00:13:57,166 --> 00:13:59,083
Okay, so...

234
00:13:59,125 --> 00:14:02,083
Could you heroes stand back a bit?

235
00:14:02,125 --> 00:14:05,166
Saber Tigers, can you tighten up
the defense around the heroes?

236
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:07,125
Stand back?

237
00:14:10,041 --> 00:14:11,125
Wh-What is that?

238
00:14:11,125 --> 00:14:13,208
Ew, gross! That's creepy!

239
00:14:19,125 --> 00:14:21,166
I'll handle the one in front.

240
00:14:21,208 --> 00:14:27,125
These are strong, so I might not have
the leeway to save the kill for the heroes.

241
00:14:27,166 --> 00:14:30,208
Then I'll deal with the second
one coming up behind it.

242
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:32,166
Will you join us, Abyss?

243
00:14:32,166 --> 00:14:33,208
Sure.

244
00:14:44,125 --> 00:14:45,208
A-Amazing!

245
00:14:49,166 --> 00:14:51,166
You're telling me to stand back...

246
00:14:52,166 --> 00:14:55,125
Abyss, some of the monsters
have changed course!

247
00:14:55,125 --> 00:14:57,000
They're after the heroes behind us!

248
00:14:57,041 --> 00:14:58,041
- Leave them to me.
- against monsters of that level?

249
00:14:58,083 --> 00:14:59,166
...against monsters of that level?

250
00:15:02,166 --> 00:15:05,166
Draconic Buster!

251
00:15:14,041 --> 00:15:18,041
My unique skill is only level four right now.

252
00:15:18,041 --> 00:15:21,041
Revise how you see me already.

253
00:15:21,125 --> 00:15:23,125
FUTURE RULER
- Behold the power of Kirihara,

254
00:15:23,125 --> 00:15:26,041
THE POWER OF KIRIHARA
- your future ruler!

255
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:31,000
That reminds me... Where are
Hijiri-san and Itsuki-san?

256
00:15:32,125 --> 00:15:34,208
Looks like something's going on over there.

257
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:37,125
Might be time for us to head back.

258
00:15:37,125 --> 00:15:41,208
These guys offed themselves the moment
we discovered them, anyway.

259
00:15:41,208 --> 00:15:46,041
I suppose that means they were spies
who'd sworn their lives to their master.

260
00:15:46,083 --> 00:15:48,125
Which country would do this, though?

261
00:15:48,166 --> 00:15:50,125
Now that's a good question.

262
00:15:50,125 --> 00:15:54,000
I think they were dispatched to do
something to those of us in 2-C...

263
00:15:54,166 --> 00:15:56,208
by the Goddess Vicius.

264
00:15:57,000 --> 00:15:59,125
At least, that's my read on them.

265
00:16:01,208 --> 00:16:04,041
I've finished preparing dinner.

266
00:16:04,041 --> 00:16:05,041
Okay.

267
00:16:05,083 --> 00:16:09,041
Thanks to Slei, we're making much
better time than we expected.

268
00:16:09,041 --> 00:16:13,000
Yes, it looks like it's not much
further to the Witch of Taboos.

269
00:16:13,125 --> 00:16:15,083
What are you looking at?

270
00:16:15,125 --> 00:16:17,208
I saw a strange light in the distance.

271
00:16:17,208 --> 00:16:20,166
I thought it might be some
monsters killing each other off.

272
00:16:21,083 --> 00:16:22,208
That's to the northeast.

273
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:24,083
The northeast?

274
00:16:24,125 --> 00:16:25,125
Oh, I see.

275
00:16:25,166 --> 00:16:28,166
The direction of Alion,
where that damn goddess lives.

276
00:16:32,208 --> 00:16:33,208
Eve?

277
00:16:34,166 --> 00:16:36,041
What is it, Seras?

278
00:16:36,166 --> 00:16:39,000
I don't see Sir Tooka anywhere.

279
00:16:39,041 --> 00:16:40,041
Or Piggymaru.

280
00:16:41,125 --> 00:16:44,125
He's not the kind of man who'd leave us

281
00:16:44,125 --> 00:16:47,166
in the middle of the Land of Monsters
without a word.

282
00:16:48,041 --> 00:16:51,041
You should already know that well.

283
00:16:51,083 --> 00:16:52,083
I do.

284
00:17:03,083 --> 00:17:04,083
You're up?

285
00:17:04,125 --> 00:17:06,125
Tooka, those monsters...

286
00:17:06,125 --> 00:17:08,166
I sensed them nearby
while you were sleeping.

287
00:17:08,208 --> 00:17:10,000
So I put them down.

288
00:17:10,041 --> 00:17:13,166
That monster... Th-That's
a human-faced beast, isn't it?

289
00:17:13,166 --> 00:17:14,125
Yeah.

290
00:17:14,166 --> 00:17:20,041
Though, compared to what I'm used to,
it wasn't particularly troublesome.

291
00:17:20,083 --> 00:17:24,041
Now I'm searching to see if it
has any ingredients I can use.

292
00:17:24,041 --> 00:17:26,166
You took a human-faced beast all by yourself?

293
00:17:26,208 --> 00:17:28,208
Am I still dreaming?

294
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:31,083
No, that's just how Sir Tooka is.

295
00:17:31,125 --> 00:17:33,208
Indeed, because we have him,

296
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:36,125
we can see a ray of hope in this plan

297
00:17:36,125 --> 00:17:40,083
to head into the nightmare that is
the heart of the Land of Monsters.

298
00:17:40,208 --> 00:17:44,041
I'm confident you can make the
impossible possible, Sir Tooka,

299
00:17:44,125 --> 00:17:45,125
but please...

300
00:17:45,166 --> 00:17:49,083
don't shoulder too much all on your own.

301
00:17:50,208 --> 00:17:54,083
Looks like it's impossible
to scale these cliffs, even with Slei.

302
00:17:54,125 --> 00:17:58,083
Hmm, that means we'll have
to follow the road along them.

303
00:17:58,208 --> 00:18:01,208
I found a path that continues through
the cliffs on the east side.

304
00:18:02,125 --> 00:18:03,166
Let's hurry that way.

305
00:18:03,166 --> 00:18:07,000
Sir Tooka, you should get some rest as well.

306
00:18:07,125 --> 00:18:09,125
The wind's growing humid.

307
00:18:09,125 --> 00:18:12,125
I want to get as far as we
can before the rains hit.

308
00:18:22,083 --> 00:18:24,166
I don't sense any monsters yet.

309
00:18:25,041 --> 00:18:27,041
This lack of monsters...

310
00:18:27,041 --> 00:18:30,208
Do you think it's because of our
proximity to the Witch of Taboos?

311
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:33,083
Are you okay?

312
00:18:33,083 --> 00:18:34,083
Yes.

313
00:18:34,125 --> 00:18:36,041
Is the Land of Monsters scary?

314
00:18:36,083 --> 00:18:39,041
I wouldn't say it hasn't been scary...

315
00:18:39,041 --> 00:18:40,166
but I'm okay.

316
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:42,208
Don't go saying anything like,

317
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:47,083
"Dying here with Eve is better than
continuing to live in Monroy."

318
00:18:47,125 --> 00:18:49,125
That isn't exactly wrong...

319
00:18:49,166 --> 00:18:52,125
but I don't believe I'm going to die here.

320
00:18:52,166 --> 00:18:58,125
Miss Seras told me that
as long as you live, Sir Tooka,

321
00:18:58,125 --> 00:19:01,208
we should reach our destination safely.

322
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:06,000
She believes in me a little too much.

323
00:19:06,208 --> 00:19:13,208
Still, thanks to her, I've held hope that
we'll be fine so long as we have you with us.

324
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:15,166
We have Slei, too.

325
00:19:17,208 --> 00:19:21,208
Both Eve and Lis have complete faith in me.

326
00:19:25,125 --> 00:19:26,125
It's fine.

327
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:28,083
I can see this through.

328
00:19:29,125 --> 00:19:32,125
I have no intention of betraying that faith.

329
00:19:43,125 --> 00:19:46,000
We were able to avoid most of the detours.

330
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:49,000
Once we're through here,
we'll be close to the witch.

331
00:19:49,125 --> 00:19:52,041
We managed to make it this far somehow.

332
00:19:52,083 --> 00:19:53,083
Indeed.

333
00:19:53,083 --> 00:19:55,000
You've done well too, Lis.

334
00:19:55,000 --> 00:19:55,208
Yeah.

335
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:59,083
I don't know how I can ever
thank you, Tooka and Seras.

336
00:19:59,083 --> 00:20:02,000
Big Sis, you're forgetting Piggymaru and Slei.

337
00:20:03,166 --> 00:20:04,208
You're right.

338
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:08,125
I owe you both my heartfelt gratitude too.

339
00:20:08,125 --> 00:20:10,083
You've been a great help.

340
00:20:10,083 --> 00:20:14,083
Well, we all needed your map too, Eve.

341
00:20:15,041 --> 00:20:16,041
I told you, right?

342
00:20:16,041 --> 00:20:18,041
I didn't help you out of goodwill alone.

343
00:20:18,083 --> 00:20:20,083
So you're saying we're even.

344
00:20:20,083 --> 00:20:22,041
You're so kind, Sir Tooka.

345
00:20:22,041 --> 00:20:23,041
Yeah.

346
00:20:23,083 --> 00:20:25,000
I don't care if our home is small,

347
00:20:25,041 --> 00:20:29,083
as long as I can live a quiet life with
Lis in a peaceful land free from war.

348
00:20:29,083 --> 00:20:32,041
The moment I thought my days
as a bloodsport warrior were over

349
00:20:32,083 --> 00:20:35,041
and that dream was finally in reach,
it was snatched from me.

350
00:20:37,083 --> 00:20:40,041
But now I have hope
for that dream once more.

351
00:20:40,125 --> 00:20:44,208
I know I talked about us starting a farm
together once this is all over,

352
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:48,000
but maybe that future
isn't so far off anymore.

353
00:20:48,041 --> 00:20:50,166
Yeah. That's true, Big Sis.

354
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:53,208
Eve.

355
00:20:55,041 --> 00:20:57,041
What? Completely out of nowhere?

356
00:20:58,000 --> 00:20:59,000
Eve, wait!

357
00:21:04,041 --> 00:21:06,125
That's not a human-faced beast, but...

358
00:21:06,125 --> 00:21:08,083
Wh-What's the matter, Tooka?

359
00:21:08,166 --> 00:21:10,208
Is that monster still breathing?

360
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:12,208
No, it seems to be dead.

361
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:14,083
It's not moving at all.

362
00:21:15,041 --> 00:21:16,041
Paralyze.

363
00:21:16,208 --> 00:21:18,208
Yeah, it's definitely dead.

364
00:21:18,208 --> 00:21:20,208
Eve made the right call.

365
00:21:20,208 --> 00:21:23,125
It caught us off guard at such close range.

366
00:21:24,041 --> 00:21:27,208
That was definitely our best
course of action, but...

367
00:21:27,208 --> 00:21:32,041
What is the intense sense of unease
I felt the moment it showed up?

368
00:21:33,208 --> 00:21:35,125
Everyone, get back!

369
00:21:35,166 --> 00:21:36,166
Don't tell me...

370
00:21:45,166 --> 00:21:49,000
Wh-What was that just now? And this...

371
00:21:49,125 --> 00:21:52,125
A heinous nature like the
embodiment of a torture device,

372
00:21:52,166 --> 00:21:55,166
malice blacker than the deepest inks,

373
00:21:56,000 --> 00:21:58,166
and a sadism darker than coal tar...

374
00:21:59,166 --> 00:22:01,000
Now I get it.

375
00:22:03,208 --> 00:22:05,125
They're closing in.

376
00:22:14,083 --> 00:22:16,000
Wh-What?

377
00:22:21,041 --> 00:22:24,041
They're flooding here from all directions.

378
00:22:25,000 --> 00:22:26,000
But there...

379
00:22:30,041 --> 00:22:34,166
There are far too many of them!

380
00:24:10,166 --> 00:24:14,208
TO THE LIMIT, AND BEYOND

